A||||11||turbo86se||Ahh! If this belt squeaks one more time!||||11||
Z||000000||turbo86se||11-06-2001||10:15 PM||||Since it's gotten cold out, my '88 V6 squeaked only at startup for a few seconds. Now it squeaks loudly everytime I stop and go! Annoying!!! I pulled on the belt, it does have some play, and the top bolt to the alternator needs to be tightened. It's a tight as I can get it with a wrench. <P>How can I fix the annoying squeek? What do i tighten? What tools will I need?<BR>I did a search, which is sweet Cliff, but didn't come up with any answers.<BR>TIA!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroMGDriver||11-07-2001||01:13 AM||||It sounds like a squeaky belt to me.  All you have to do is get some kind of prybar like a large screwdriver and find where you can get some leverage while tightening the adjustment bolt.  Two people might help.<P>------------------<BR>www4.ncsu.edu/~mgdickey/fiero.html||||reg||1
Z||000002||NEO Cesek Racing||11-07-2001||03:29 AM||||hey man i feel ya. i've had exactly the same problem and it's annoying (not to mention embarassing) especially when you pull up to a red light next to some hot chics lol. i'm gonna get the crow bar out tomorrow morning, i'll post later on to tell you how mine goes. good luck.<P><P>------------------<BR>I used to have a handle <BR>on life but it broke.||||reg||1
Z||000003||NEO Cesek Racing||11-07-2001||03:51 AM||||ps: if you've got the cash, you can order a belt tensioner from the fiero store catalogue or the website. they cost around $60 but i guess it makes the one man operation a little easier. i'm too cheap to buy one so the crow bar will have to do.<P>------------------<BR>I used to have a handle <BR>on life but it broke.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||11-07-2001||08:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>Since it's gotten cold out, my '88 V6 squeaked only at startup for a few seconds. Now it squeaks loudly everytime I stop and go! Annoying!!! I pulled on the belt, it does have some play, and the top bolt to the alternator needs to be tightened. It's a tight as I can get it with a wrench. <P>How can I fix the annoying squeek? What do i tighten? What tools will I need?<BR>I did a search, which is sweet Cliff, but didn't come up with any answers.<BR>TIA!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you plan on tightening the belt, why not replace it as well...<BR>A new belt at the proper tention does wonders...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||11-07-2001||10:03 AM||||If my belt squeeked that much, I would have taken a knife to it by now and replaced it with a new one.  Using a knife is a theroputic accessory to use.  I wouldn't have a clean shot with my .45  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art 4..s..money. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4money.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||11-07-2001||01:13 PM||||I highly recommend using the $7 belt tightener tool from Harbor Fright <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Looks like a turnbuckle type of thing, that you prop between the crank pulley and accessory (e.g. -  alternator) pulley.  Turn the threaded thingy in the middle until the belt is properly tensioned; tighten the adjustment bolt.  Remove the tool.  Works like a charm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||NEO Cesek Racing||11-07-2001||02:14 PM||||hey i went in and tightened my alt belt with the crow bar. no more squeek.  but then my dumb@$$ left the key in the ignition turned on and the dome light on while i went inside and got ready for work for about 20 minutes or so  (i was workin on my headlight motor afterwards). <BR>now my volt meter sits right around 14 instead of 16. just hope i didn't kill my alternator again.  oh well we'll see. hope you get yers to quiet down.<P>------------------<BR>I used to have a handle <BR>on life but it broke.||||reg||1
Z||000008||K2m4||11-07-2001||02:55 PM||||Man Everyone would of had a chucke at my contraption i rigged together for tensioning the v belt. It was a broom handle and a snow shovel that i had propped and balanced against the garage door . I wish I snapped a picture but when all was said and done i had a perfectly torgued belt on my GT. my naighbor got a chuckle out of it. i invited him over to look at what i had done. He always helped me in the past with a bar on the alternator while im underneath torqing the bolt.   Ingenuity at its best  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2m4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jncomutt||11-07-2001||05:41 PM||||The belt on my 84 4cyl squeaks too.  It does it for like 2 seconds when I first start it, just as yours did.  And it doesn't do it all the time.  Someone had mentioned to me that it might by the AC belt?  Could I remove this belt??  (My AC doesn't work, I tried charging it, the front side holds pressure but I can't manage to fill the system)  And if I remove the belt, will there be any difference in how the car runs???<P>I don't care about the AC, so if its gone, oh well.<P>Or is it most likely just the Alt. belt||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric_PA||11-07-2001||05:53 PM||||I got tired of my belt always squealing and having to constantly replace them. I had a bent alt. bracket. So what did I do to fix it, I took the 2.8 out and replaced it with a 3800. No more problems now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I always eneded up having to tighten it myself, so I would crank the bolt somewhat tight, then go on top of the car, pry it a bit, then go back under and tighten it the rest of the way. It was normal procedure before I left work to get home. Not the best way, especially when it rained, but would get me home.||||reg||8
Z||000011||reddog||11-08-2001||09:04 PM||||Well I know you've probably heard it before and it sounds like a stupid idea. But get a bar of soap and press it against the underside of the belt as the car idles. I tried everything to stop mine including changing both belts and tightened them on 4 different occassions but nothing worked longer than 24 hours. Finally I got fed up and tried the soap thing and I'll be damned if it didn't clear right up. It's been about a month now and still no squeal. It sounded dumb but it really worked for my GT maybe it will work for you. BTW stay away from the belt dressing stuff that you can buy at the parts store. I't doesn't work and actually makes it worse after a while. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">:<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/on_fire_trail.gif"> ||||reg||1
